{"text": "Operations 44 English Operations 2. Fill the water tank with potable water. Remove the cap and pour water. NOTE Before using the water tank for the first time, clean the water tank thoroughly, especially the nozzle. Regularly clean the water tank and the nozzle. 3. Reinsert the water tank and close the door. Make sure the water outlet of the water tank faces forward. 4. Put a water glass under the water outlet (cid:8) (cid:7) (cid:30)(cid:48) (cid:38)(cid:48) (cid:54) (cid:45) (cid:3)(cid:4) (cid:34) (cid:32) (cid:43) (cid:32) (cid:48) (cid:34) (cid:34) (cid:48) (cid:47) (cid:48) of the dispenser, and gently push the dispenser lever to dispense water. (cid:26)(cid:30)(cid:49)(cid:34)(cid:47) CAUTION \u2022 The water dispenser is designed to dispense potable water. Fill the water tank only with potable water. Do not fill with any other liquids. \u2022 Do not fill the water tank excessively, which causes an overflow. \u2022 Do not try to fill the water tank without removing it from the door. \u2022 Make sure that water tank is seated properly. \u2022 Do not use the refrigerator without the water tank. This may reduce performance and efficiency. \u2022 To prevent water bouncing, make sure the glass is in line with the dispenser lever. NOTE To secure more room, you can use the water tank to store food. In this case, remove the lid of the tank. Untitled-8 44 2023-03-29 (cid:31)(cid:31) 2:24:14", "source": "D:\\Study\\4_Forth Semester\\AI\\project\\MultiAgent_RAG\\data\\Top Mounted Freezer Twist Ice Maker 391L user_manual.pdf", "page": 43}